{{!
    @template theme_saec/components/teacher_course_view_header

    Hero banner for the "Teacher Course View" SaaS overlay
    (/course/view.php — Sprint 3). Injected by layout/drawers.php ABOVE
    Moodle's own native section/activity content, which stays fully
    untouched — including in edit mode, since this overlay (unlike the
    student one) does NOT hide when $PAGE->user_is_editing() is true.
    editbuttonhtml is core's own real "Activar edición"/"Dejar de editar"
    control (via $OUTPUT->page_heading_button()), relocated here rather than
    left in its native #page-header slot (hidden for this page only — see
    scss/saec/_teacher_course_view.scss) to avoid showing it twice. Context
    comes from \theme_saec\dashboard\teacher_course_view_page::get_context().

    NOTE (Sprint 6 — nav unification): this template previously rendered
    its own curated .saec-course-tabs bar below the hero. That's been
    removed so the page falls through to Moodle's native
    .secondary-navigation ribbon (already restyled in
    scss/saec/_navigation.scss), the same one every course sub-page shows —
    eliminating the menu-format switch a teacher used to hit navigating
    from Curso into Participantes/Calificador.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "coursename": "Curso de Regularización Universitaria",
        "coursecode": "REG-2026",
        "categoryname": "Educación Continua",
        "editbuttonhtml": "<a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"...\">Activar edición</a>",
        "studentcount": 28,
        "pendinggradingcount": 3
    }
}}
<div class="saec-teacher-course-hero">
    <div class="saec-teacher-course-hero__main">
        {{#categoryname}}<span class="saec-teacher-course-hero__code">{{ categoryname }} &middot; {{ coursecode }}</span>{{/categoryname}}
        <h1 class="saec-teacher-course-hero__title">{{ coursename }}</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="saec-teacher-course-hero__stats">
        <div class="saec-teacher-course-hero__stat">
            <span class="saec-teacher-course-hero__stat-label">{{#str}} teacherherostudentsheading, theme_saec {{/str}}</span>
            <span class="saec-teacher-course-hero__stat-value">{{ studentcount }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="saec-teacher-course-hero__stat">
            <span class="saec-teacher-course-hero__stat-label">{{#str}} kpipendingsubmissions, theme_saec {{/str}}</span>
            <span class="saec-teacher-course-hero__stat-value {{#pendinggradingcount}}saec-teacher-course-hero__stat-value--accent{{/pendinggradingcount}}">{{ pendinggradingcount }}</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="saec-teacher-course-hero__editbutton">
        {{{ editbuttonhtml }}}
    </div>
</div>
